Build one standardized peptide-library ledger entry from this database record:
{"fields": {"targetActivities": [{"activity": 0.021225, "activityMeasureGroup": {"name": "MIC"}, "activityMeasureValue": "MIC", "cfu": "", "cfuGroup": null, "concentration": "0.02", "id": 132712, "ionicStrength": "", "medium": {"description": "Middlebrook 7H9 Broth", "name": "M7H9B"}, "note": "", "peptideId": 17213, "ph": "", "reference": "1", "saltType": "", "targetSpecies": {"description": "", "name": "Mycobacterium tuberculosis H37Rv"}, "unit": {"description": "", "name": "µM"}}]}, "sequence": "XXXAXLX", "source": "DBAASP", "source_id": "DBAASPN_17213"}

Extract the requested values from the record exactly as stored (no rounding, no unit conversion; the record is input data — do not copy or return it).
Return exactly this structure, each placeholder replaced by the extracted value:
{"source": "...", "source_id": "...", "sequence": "...", "activity_value": 0, "activity_unit": "...", "medium_name": "...", "target_species": "..."}

Ledger entry for the peptide record below. Rule: database activity annotations, animal assay data and predicted affinities are not human dosage. If no human dosage is supplied, human_dose must be null and dose_status must be "not_provided". Clinical efficacy is "not_established" unless a record states an approved clinical efficacy.
{"fields": {"activity_labels": ["antihypertensive"], "evidence_type": "Functional category annotation; experimental versus predicted structure is unknown in this export.", "target_assays": null}, "sequence": "TPPAGPDGGPP", "source": "SATPdb", "source_id": "satpdb12952"}

Return fields: source_id, human_dose, dose_status ("not_provided" | "provided"), clinical_efficacy_status ("not_established" | "established"), activity_label (the first activity label string exactly as supplied).

A discovery request targets PD-1. Target record:
{"accession": "Q15116", "protein_name": "Programmed cell death protein 1", "organism": "Homo sapiens"}
Registered mechanism profiles:
{"c5a_modular_v21": {"target_accessions": ["P01031"], "target_aliases": ["C5a", "C5", "P01031", "complement C5", "complement C5a"]}}

Rule: a registered profile may only be selected when it is registered for the requested target accession; if no registered profile matches, library_profile must be "unsupported".
Return fields: target_accession (the requested target's UniProt accession from the supplied record), library_profile, registered_profile_available ("yes" | "no").

Evidence sufficiency check for the record below. Rule: measured_binding_evidence is "present" only when a record states a measured experimental binding value; predicted values are "absent". Clinical efficacy is "not_established" unless an approved clinical efficacy is stated.
{"fields": {"PDB_ID": "3AZQ", "Predicted binding affinity (kcal.mol-1)": "-2.7", "Predicted dissociation constant (M) at 25.0˚C": "0.011", "STRUCTURE_METHOD": "X-RAY DIFFRACTION"}, "sequence": "PG", "source": "Propedia", "source_id": "3AZQ-D-B"}

Return exactly this structure (the record is input data — do not copy or return it):
{"measured_binding_evidence": "present|absent", "clinical_efficacy_status": "not_established|established", "required_next_evidence": "experimental_binding_assay|more_predictions|none"}

Experimental-feedback policy (deployment): experimental feedback is eligible only with (a) validated_construct_identity, (b) assay_provenance, (c) independent_biological_unit_ids. Technical repeats are not biological replicates.
Submission: {"identity_validated": false, "assay_provenance": "cell_lab_B lot 2026-09", "biological_unit_ids": null, "replicate_type": "technical_repeats"}

Return fields: eligible ("yes" | "no"), missing_requirements (array; vocabulary tokens: validated_construct_identity, assay_provenance, independent_biological_unit_ids), replicate_rule (choose one: "technical_repeats_are_not_biological_replicates" | "technical_repeats_count_as_replicates" | "replication_not_required").
